  "page1": {
    "title": "The Bookkeeping of a Falling Ball",
    "subtitle": "Why energy is never lost, only moved around.",
    "body": "Lift a heavy book onto a high shelf, and you have done something the universe quietly records. Physicists describe that effort as <u>work</u>, which simply means a force acting over a distance. The work you spent lifting the book has not vanished. It has been deposited into the book as stored energy, a hidden account waiting to be drawn upon. Because of its height, the book now holds what we call potential energy, energy of position rather than of motion. Raise it twice as high, and you have stored twice as much, ready to be released the instant it is let go.\n\nLet the book slip off the shelf, and the account is suddenly spent. As the book falls, its height shrinks while its speed grows, and the stored potential energy is steadily turned into the energy of movement, called kinetic energy. The remarkable thing is the bookkeeping: at every instant of the fall, <u>the amount of potential energy lost is exactly matched by the kinetic energy gained</u>. Their sum never changes. The falling book is simply moving money between two accounts that always hold the same total. This is the heart of the <mark>conservation</mark> of energy, the principle that energy can be transformed from one form into another but can never be created or destroyed.\n\nAt first this seems to clash with everyday experience, since a bouncing ball clearly loses height with each bounce and finally stops. But the energy has not disappeared. It has merely scattered into forms we overlook, mostly heat and faint sound spread thinly into the floor and the air. Trace those subtle forms carefully, and the books balance again, down to the last fraction. So whenever energy appears to go missing, a physicist does not assume it is gone; she assumes she has simply failed to follow where it chose to <blank>.",
    "illustration": "../../assets/illustrations/2026-07-Sun/05.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "As a book falls, height becomes speed; the energy total never changes.",
    "gloss_extra": [
      {
        "term": "potential energy",
        "ko": "위치 에너지"
      },
      {
        "term": "kinetic energy",
        "ko": "운동 에너지"
      },
      {
        "term": "bookkeeping",
        "ko": "장부 정리, 회계"
      }
    ]
  },
